## Phase 0 — Foundation

- [ ] `git init`; commit the untouched starter as the first commit
- [ ] Add `pyproject.toml` (black line-length 88, isort `profile=black`, mypy settings,
      pytest + coverage config) and a matching `.flake8` — black's 88 and flake8's
      default 79 contradict each other until this exists
- [ ] Run `black .` and `isort .`; clear all 51 flake8 errors
- [ ] Commit the clean baseline separately, so later diffs show only real work

## Phase 1 — Define the application

- [ ] Write the app's purpose and feature list into `README.md`
- [ ] Decide the task data model: id, description, priority, status, due date, tags,
      created_at, completed_at

## Phase 2 — Features (4 beyond basic CRUD)

- [ ] **Strategy** — `utils/sorting.py`: sort/filter by priority, due date, status
- [ ] **Factory** — `utils/exporters.py`: export to JSON, CSV, Markdown
- [ ] **Command** — `utils/commands.py`: undo/redo for add, complete, delete
- [ ] **Observer** — `utils/events.py`: event log and notifications on task changes
- [ ] Extend `TaskManager`: due dates, tags, search, priority validation, status enum
- [ ] **CLI** — replace the demo `main.py` with a `click` app (`click` is already in
      `requirements.txt` and currently unused); this is what makes it an application
      rather than a script

## Phase 3 — Testing and quality

- [ ] Unit tests for every new module — happy path, edge cases, and error conditions
      (invalid priority, empty export, undo on an empty stack, corrupt JSON, missing file)
- [ ] Make the CLI testable via `click.testing.CliRunner` so `main.py` is not a 0% hole
- [ ] Drive total coverage above 90% (rubric requires >80%)
- [ ] Run `bandit` for the security-practices bonus

## Phase 4 — Documentation

- [ ] `docs/ai_edit_log.md` — at least 5 entries in the template's format, capturing
      real prompts, rejected suggestions, and bugs found in AI-generated code
- [ ] `docs/final_report.md` from `docs/report_template.md`, 1000–1500 words, including
      why each design pattern was chosen
- [ ] Rewrite `README.md`: features, CLI usage examples, setup, dependencies
- [ ] Add `LICENSE.txt` (README already links to it, but it does not exist)
- [ ] Generate and keep the HTML coverage report

## Phase 5 — Final verification

- [ ] `black . && isort . && flake8 . && mypy . && pytest --cov=. --cov-report=html`
      passes clean
- [ ] Review the full codebase against `ai_guidance/code_review_checklist.md`
